begin{aligned}n & =2{q}^{8}+14{q}^{4}-4 \\\\  & =2({{field-2}}-2) \\\\  & ={{field-3}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=${{field-4}} is an integer." :question/worked-solution "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nNotice that all terms in the expression $2{q}^{8}+14{q}^{4}-4$ have a common factor of $2.$ \n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is $\\text{even}$ since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =2{q}^{8}+14{q}^{4}-4 \\\\  & =2({{{q}^{8}+7{q}^{4}-2}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a={q}^{8}+7{q}^{4}-2$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ee426ac-48be-52e8-a0bb-b48b9087cf97" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Parity of Non-Linear Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "197f6f2b-20c1-5ffc-859c-7547e9d1715d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{m}^{5}+24{m}^{4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406997} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8d43fe-572c-52fa-87ce-f0a18a2a9a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{m}^{5}+4{m}^{4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407035} {:answer/id #uuid "f10f3b03-8227-5565-86cf-79b2043899ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{m}^{5}+4{m}^{4}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d8d43fe-572c-52fa-87ce-f0a18a2a9a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{m}^{5}+4{m}^{4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407035} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fab608f-053d-5ee1-a76f-366dc128bea6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407070} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ceecaee-fc92-5b68-b9e1-ac413b6e598e" :