 {:answer/id #uuid "3a11f8f5-0a39-5261-8f79-73741befb47c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterexample" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412520} :answer-field/id #uuid "99dfee88-dfe0-58a1-8612-fb8206ae22c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412615} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80293b1d-10bc-5497-b2e7-2fc622ce4bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "prove" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412544} {:answer/id #uuid "a1056cdb-e9cc-5a85-bfb3-0a2f5c17636a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "disprove" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1056cdb-e9cc-5a85-bfb3-0a2f5c17636a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "disprove" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412559} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6f22d6f-482f-5f8a-bf60-63d26ce12b81" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14a28651-1999-5962-91ed-994e095a457d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412504} {:answer/id #uuid "6057e1ad-3e74-55ac-b65c-2f66b10aca81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412536} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e25bbe-943d-53f4-b3d4-7dfe8bad278e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3e25bbe-943d-53f4-b3d4-7dfe8bad278e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412576} :answer-field/id #uuid "dab95909-e45b-53f1-bf4f-61cf81c795fb" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbf3d356-bb6f-5d45-9a65-7f6a6ff861ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-221834" :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\n${x}^{2}+5x+6\\ge 0$ for any $x\\in R.$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a {{field-2}}. \nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}}\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+5x+6{{field-4}}0.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=$ {{field-5}} into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5x+6 & ={({{field-6}})}^{2}+5({{field-7}})+6 \\\\  & ={{field-8}} \\\\  & {{field-9}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x=$ {{field-10}} is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in R,\\,{x}^{2}+5x+6\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n¬(∀x\\in R,\\,{x}^{2}+5x+6\\ge 0)\\,≡\\,∃x\\in R,\\,{x}^{2}+5x+6<0\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists a real number $x$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+5x+6<0.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $x=-2.5$ suffices:\n\nBy substituting $x=-2.5$ into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5x+6 & =(-2.5)^{2}+5(-2.5)+6 \\\\  & =-0.25 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $x=-2.5$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0e960a4-872c-55c0-8